<title>EGYPT: Egypt pound interbank market quiet after holidays.</title>
<headline>Egypt pound interbank market quiet after holidays.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1997-05-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>The private sector overnight interbank market on the Egyptian pound ranged from 7-3/4 to 9-1/2 percent on Sunday, the first day of trade after a three-day long weekend, bankers said.</p>
<p>One week rates were put at between 8 and 8-3/4 percent in the market they described as quiet.</p>
<p>Bankers also said that public sector banks had kept their minimum lending rate steady at 10-1/2 percent.</p>
<p>$1 = 3.395 pounds</p>
<p>-- Cairo newsroom +202 578 3290/1</p>
